; TALK.J entry 4 (LZSS-packed)
;
; What Merlin says at the start of a turn (Board_Task step 3201): on a CPU player's turn, and only
; while g_optSkipCpuTalk is 0, which the game never sets (scripts/README.md).
; $entry (TurnStart_PickScript):
; 0 the first month
; 1 assets at 7/8 of the goal
; 2 last at the start of the round, first now
; 3 first at the start of the round, last now
; 4 ahead: a rival store it can't afford
; 5 ahead: a rival store in a chain of 4
; 6 ahead: a rival store closed, without goods
; 7 ahead: its own store without goods
; 8 the bank on the next square
; 9 ranked better than at the start of the round
; 10 ranked worse
; 11 ahead: a rival store in a chain
; 12 ahead: a vacant lot
; 13 ahead: a rival store costing over 1/4 of its money
; 14 ahead: the bank
; 15 none of its stores ahead
; 16 ahead: its own store with free goods slots
; 17 no direction (after the bank)
; 18 no direction, on an elevator square
; 19 none of these
;
; The code picks row $entry * 3 + (random 3) of the table: the offset of a text, the
; portrait's face and the voice's XA channel. It shows the speaker's name and that text in
; the talk panel, the portrait (face, at a random position), plays the voice, and waits for
; cross (30 frames at most). Table comments: entry.variant situation: what is said.
;
; What it says: "[<player>]"
;
; 2384 bytes on the disc. Written by `tools/tss.py extract`; `make scripts` (`tools/tss.py build`)
; assembles the scripts into the disc's files again, in scripts/build/.
    $v00 = random 1
    $v01 = random 3
    $v02 = random 3
    talk_speaker PLAYER
    talk_clear
    talk "【%NMY】"                         ; [<player>]
    talk "%K"
    $v04 = $entry
    $v04 *= 3
    $v04 += $v02
    $v04 *= 3
    $l0 = table_0090[$v04]
    $v04 += 1
    $l1 = table_0090[$v04]
    $v04 += 1
    $l2 = table_0090[$v04]
    talk_data $l0
    talk_show 0
    talk_open
    portrait_show unused=$v00, face=$l1, pos=$v01
    talk_wait_open
    play_xa 4, $l2                        ; voice: XA track 4 * 16 + $l2 (g_xaSets[1])
    yield
    wait_buttons_for CROSS|0x300, 30      ; wait for cross, 30 frames at most
    portrait_hide 0
    talk_close
    talk_wait_closed
    end

